# nr-office-comrs-excel-read: the workbook reader of mixdog-office-com (src/excel/{mod,cells,numfmt,styles,validation,snapshot,page,selection,issues}.rs,
# src/excel/edit/mod.rs (an empty stub for nr-office-comrs-excel-edit), tests/excel_read.rs, tests/excel_read_live.rs,
# recorder/scenarios/excel-read.json).
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave). No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name and no new dependency belong to this task:
# the crate already depends on regex, serde_json and the workspace crates the reader uses.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs (not owned by this task)
Add to the `pub mod` block (next to `pub mod drivers;`):

    pub mod excel;

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/drivers.rs (not owned by this task)
In the `READERS` table add the line (Excel's reader answers both the whole read and the paged read, the rule of `format::excel_reads_a_page` chooses):

    ("xlsx", &crate::excel::Reader),

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test targets, after `[[test]] name = "actions_live"`:

    [[test]]
    name = "excel_read"
    path = "tests/excel_read.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "excel_read_live"
    path = "tests/excel_read_live.rs"

## 4. What nr-office-comrs-excel-edit takes over
`src/excel/edit/mod.rs` is declared by `src/excel/mod.rs` as `pub(crate) mod edit;` and is an empty module. The editor task replaces it, adds its own
`("xlsx", &crate::excel::edit::Editor)` line to `EDITORS`, and reads from the reader's modules what it shares (all `pub(crate)`):
`excel::cells` (`ps_of`: a COM value as the PowerShell value), `excel::numfmt` (`excel_word`, `ColorNames`, `color_names`: the Korean colour table and the
once-per-host language read that `Set-ExcelNumberFormat` also needs, `COLOR_KEYS`, `english_number_format`). The colour-section pattern
`\[(Black|Blue|Cyan|Green|Magenta|Red|White|Yellow|Color(\d{1,2}))\]` of `Set-ExcelNumberFormat` is the editor's: define it there.

## 5. Nothing in SERVICE_PENDING, no protocol file, no Cargo.lock line.
